I take it that boots of levitation have some chance
of autocursing?

My pet stomped across some boots in an armor shop
with no complaint, so I tried them on.

Suddenly I was floating, only to find out that the
boots that went on so easily came off not at all,
like a Chinese finger puzzle.

If I hadn't just fifty turns or so earlier prayed to
my god for food, I might have tried a prayer to get
the boots uncursed.

Instead, too impatient to wait out the problem, what
with cavepersons starting the game foodless and me
having found none so far, and as a cavewoman who had
managed to enchant her sling up to +6, I committed a
stylish suicide by pegging rocks at the shopkeeper
until s/he offed me with a wand of magic missile.

I did manage to die still a vegan, it happened,
having managed to outrun my pet only to the lichen
corpses.

Thence I moved onward to the next game.

Die and learn.

xanthian.

